/-!
# Geometric irreducibility and purely transcendental extensions

Geometric irreducibility of an extension of fields `B/A` is Mathlib's
`AlgebraicGeometry.GeometricallyIrreducible` for the morphism `Spec B ⟶ Spec A`: for every field
extension `F/A` the space `Spec (B ⊗[A] F)` is irreducible.

Let `K/k` be an extension of fields. Then `K/k` is geometrically irreducible if and only if the
induced extension `K(X)/k(X)` of purely transcendental extensions in one variable is, where
`k⟮X⟯ = RatFunc k`.

Let `K/L/M` be a tower of fields with `L` geometrically irreducible over `M`, and let `x : K` be
transcendental over `L`. Then `L(x)` is geometrically irreducible over `M(x)`, the two fields being
taken inside `K`: the base is `M⟮x⟯` and the extension is the `M⟮x⟯`-subfield of `K` generated by
the image of `L`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.GeometricallyIrreducible.iff_ratFunc`: `K/k` is geometrically irreducible
  if and only if `K(X)/k(X)` is.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.geometricallyIrreducible_specMap_adjoin_of_transcendental`: `L(x)/M(x)` is
  geometrically irreducible when `L/M` is and `x` is transcendental over `L`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G31](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G31)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G32](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G32)
-/

